# The pictures of mechanisms.md: a box and a lid linked, the lid set to
# move in a mechanism and hinged on the box's back edge, then swung
# open; the hinge made a driven one, opened to 60° in the parameter
# table. Then a ball joint between two plates and the plate's freedom;
# a four-bar whose bars lie on top of each other assembling once they
# are set to move (fourbar_stacked.tlspr); the driven lid of
# boxlid.tlspr dragged open and on past its range; the four-bar's
# coupler turned with Ctrl.
file $testdata/ui/mechanism/host.tlspr
menu File|Open...
file $testdata/ui/mechanism/box.tlspr
menu Assembly|Link / Assemble...
file $testdata/ui/mechanism/lid.tlspr
menu Assembly|Link / Assemble...
view rotated
key f
click-tw moves in a mechanism
cursor off
shot mechanisms-1-parts both
# The view turned to look from behind, where the back edges show: the
# box's top one, then the lid's bottom one.
move 300 300
down M 300 300
move 500 300 M
move 700 300 M
up M 700 300
key f
click-entity 80030037
click-entity 8004003a
shot mechanisms-2-edges gw
menu Assembly|Mate Hinge
key esc
view rotated
key f
shot mechanisms-3-closed gw
# The lid's front edge pulled up: it swings open about the hinge.
cursor on
move 480 268
down L 480 268
move 480 240 L
move 478 210 L
move 474 180 L
move 468 150 L
move 460 120 L
move 450 95 L
shot mechanisms-4-open gw
up L 450 95
key esc
# The drag and the hinge taken back, and the hinge made again, driven.
key z ctrl
key z ctrl
move 300 300
down M 300 300
move 500 300 M
move 700 300 M
up M 700 300
key f
click-entity 80030037
click-entity 8004003a
menu Assembly|Mate Hinge, Driven
key esc
view rotated
key f
menu Edit|Parameters...
click-tw [edit]
edit 60
cursor off
shot mechanisms-5-driven both
# A ball joint: two plates, the top circles of their holes picked and
# made a ball mate; the second plate set to move, its screen says how.
size tw 800 600
answer no
file $testdata/ui/screw_pair.tlspr
menu File|Open...
view rotated
key f
menu Sketch|Anywhere In 3d
cursor on
click-entity 80030045
click-entity 80040045
shot mechanisms-6-ball-circles gw
menu Assembly|Mate Ball
click-tw g004-b
click-tw moves in a mechanism
cursor off
mark 28 202 600 22 tw
shot mechanisms-7-ball-freedom both
# Parts need no start position: four bars linked on top of each other
# and hinged in a loop, but fixed, so the loop can't close; set to move,
# they assemble.
answer no
file $testdata/ui/mechanism/fourbar_stacked.tlspr
menu File|Open...
view rotated
key f
mark 90 212 150 22 tw
shot mechanisms-8-stacked both
click-tw g004-crank
click-tw moves in a mechanism
click-tw home
click-tw g005-coupler
click-tw moves in a mechanism
click-tw home
click-tw g006-rocker
click-tw moves in a mechanism
view rotated
key f
mark 28 162 760 62 tw
shot mechanisms-9-assembled both
# The lid on its driven hinge dragged open: angle follows, then stops at
# the range's 110.
answer no
